Given my analysis, I'm confident the answer is YES.

The key argument: The four excenters determine the four sides (as lines) of the quadrilateral. Each side is a common tangent to three of the four excircles. The common tangent to three circles (on specified sides) is unique. Therefore, the four sides are uniquely determined, and so are the four vertices and the perimeter.

\boxed{Yes}
